# rungun: set frame buffer CRAM clock to 48MHz

- Source URL: https://github.com/jotego/jtcores/issues/1257

CRAM access on Pocket has a ~3ns slack when operated at 96MHz. It is not necessary to operate it at full speed for the frame buffer operation. Modify the module so it can work with the core at 96MHz and the external CRAM at 48MHz.

## Fetched Issue/PR Details

Title: rungun: set frame buffer CRAM clock to 48MHz (#1257)

Description: The issue describes a timing constraint problem with CRAM access on Pocket hardware. There is approximately 3 nanoseconds of slack when operating at 96MHz, creating a performance bottleneck. The proposed solution is to modify the module so the core can continue operating at 96MHz while reducing the external CRAM clock speed to 48MHz, eliminating the timing violation while maintaining adequate functionality for frame buffer operations.

